I'm being klunu'i, not giving into your malmerko ideas of... no, j/k,
actually that's just when happens to be convenient for me.  I'm doing
it again tonight, BTW (if it works, that is):

http://www.blogtalkradio.com/stela-selckiku/2010/10/12/fliba-ca-lo-prulamcte-i-ao-snada-ca-lo-cabycte

It's quite easy, and free (though you do get what you pay for), to do
a show on blogtalkradio, so perhaps someone else would like to host a
show at some other time?  You just need a phone and an internet
connected computer (to run the switchboard and let callers join the
show).  I'd probably be able to call in and help if you'd like; it'd
be easier for me to just call in at another time than to host a show
then.  (If there's people doing things here I could just go for a walk
and call from my cell, for instance.)

It'd be very interesting if we had even more Lojbanic air time.  I'm
doing 3.5 hours a week on la tcati tcika, plus some YouTube and
Cinchcast, so I guess that leaves about 164 hours/week to fill before
it'd be literally impossible to consume all the Lojbanic content being
produced! :)

I'm thinking of making a new list for both announcing and discussing
internet radio shows and calling it "snakarni", what do you think?

Oh BTW I guess I came up with "snakarni", audio periodical.  Seemed
obvious enough.  I've just been calling the audience the "jundi", but
perhaps they could be "snakarnyju'i" more specifically.  What's a good
word for the host?  I guess "selvi'e" (se vitke) would be an OK
calque, or perhaps "gidva".  Any other ideas?  I'd also like a word in
the style of "snegu'e" (dreamland) that means "radioland"!  Nothing
with "cradi" though!  There's no "cradi" involved except the wireless
internet I'm using! :P

